17. Important interpretation rule
============================================================

Do not say "social valence affects agents" unless:
- between-condition divergence exceeds neutral noise floor, and
- at least one practical robustness threshold is crossed.

Acceptable conclusions:
- "Strong evidence of interactional robustness failure in model X under condition Y for task layer B."
- "Weak evidence; effect appears in efficiency but not in final state or policy adherence."
- "No reliable effect beyond neutral noise floor in this pilot."
- "Tool-call reliability was insufficient, so scientific claims cannot be made."

Do not overclaim from small samples.
Do not hide failed preflight.
Do not hide malformed tool calls.
Do not hide null results.